<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>DW - English for Africa</title><subtitle type="html">News, Analysis and Service from Germany and Europe - in 30 Languages</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-africa</id><updated>2026-11-10T16:31:03Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-africa" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/s-12756?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-africa" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Controversial kinship: From colonial rule to the Holocaust?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8a9f3d5e84ef4570563b7e229b4af6215519f7d2b4af2842418eaf4bc2793da0</id><updated>2026-11-10T16:30:05Z</updated><published>2026-11-10T15:49:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/controversial-kinship-from-colonial-rule-to-the-holocaust/a-79902228--16129c6452e2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/controversial-kinship-from-colonial-rule-to-the-holocaust/a-79902228?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Hitler once called Eastern Europe "Germany's India." A new exhibition examines the links between colonialism and Nazism, and the bitter debate over where comparisons illuminate history and where they fall short.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>DR Congo: 66 soldiers sentenced to death for 'cowardice' in conflict with FRN rebels</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:00491191b344c1b3f6032f43301a6c581289d07848c6cdd23f5eef1577cbef0f</id><updated>2026-11-10T16:30:38Z</updated><published>2026-11-10T09:43:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/dr-congo-66-soldiers-sentenced-to-death-for-cowardice-in-conflict-with-frn-rebels/a-79906794--651090ee3cc2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/dr-congo-66-soldiers-sentenced-to-death-for-cowardice-in-conflict-with-frn-rebels/a-79906794?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Dozens of defendants were put on trial over accusations that they abandoned their posts and refused to follow direct orders.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Africa's fight against fake news: Who decides what's true?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9c72e8aad00a984a0312a4f46dd5100ff4a2d176654f29fc682b246e22f5520f</id><updated>2026-11-10T16:31:03Z</updated><published>2026-11-09T15:56:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/africa-s-fight-against-fake-news-who-decides-what-s-true/a-79874039--da5aa4e49d00.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/africa-s-fight-against-fake-news-who-decides-what-s-true/a-79874039?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">From Ghana to Mozambique, the fight against fake news keeps gaining momentum. But combating disinformation also requires safeguards for free speech, leaving some governments in an inconvenient position.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Many killed after migrant boat sinks off Senegal</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e7b9408f55367fb3f63737617b1a0ca68c2ffc6dc65bf7d7083250c70e3ebec3</id><updated>2026-11-10T16:29:17Z</updated><published>2026-11-08T19:12:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/many-killed-after-migrant-boat-sinks-off-senegal/a-79890883--2975c49621fb.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/many-killed-after-migrant-boat-sinks-off-senegal/a-79890883?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The incident occurred near Kebemer off the coast of northwestern Senegal. Authorities on El Hierro in the Canary Islands have declared an emergency after a marked increase in migrant boat arrivals.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>South Africa elections: ANC marks its worst-ever performance</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:21638d9fb1dc2787ab5f4cb651188c41005208f4b136fb37d1411b08b9199f6b</id><updated>2026-11-10T16:29:17Z</updated><published>2026-11-08T17:35:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/south-africa-elections-anc-marks-its-worst-ever-performance/a-79887482--98e867ce01e0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/south-africa-elections-anc-marks-its-worst-ever-performance/a-79887482?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The African National Congress, the party of late liberation icon Nelson Mandela, slumped to its worst-ever result in South Africa's municipal election. Voters blame the ANC for water and electricity shortages.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Ebola: Why is there still no vaccine?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9c03b828ba4f5418d59d2708b1d7acda9259560bad3b2510db364e2623033c2f</id><updated>2026-11-10T16:29:17Z</updated><published>2026-11-07T21:03:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ebola-why-is-there-still-no-vaccine/a-79888134--134cc892a91f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ebola-why-is-there-still-no-vaccine/a-79888134?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Ebola has been known about for decades, but there is still no vaccine against the Bundibugyo strain of the virus causing the current outbreak. New research raises hopes of protection against the various types of Ebola.</summary><category term="World" /></entry></feed>
